"324", "400", "361"], "answer": "325", "explanation": "324, 361, and 400 are whole numbers multiplied by themselves. 325 lies between 18² and 19².", "sources": ["Derived by integer arithmetic"], "id": "odd-one-out-49", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside Africa in this atlas?", "options": ["Haiti", "Morocco", "Mauritania", "Burundi"], "answer": "Haiti", "explanation": "Haiti is grouped in North America; the other three are in Africa. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/ha.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/mo.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/mr.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/by.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-50", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('odd-one-out',10,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside Asia in this atlas?", "options": ["Afghanistan", "Turkmenistan", "Sudan", "Syria"], "answer": "Sudan", "explanation": "Sudan is grouped in Africa; the other three are in Asia. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-asia/af.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-asia/tx.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/su.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/sy.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-51", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which number is NOT a perfect square?", "options": ["441", "361", "400", "362"], "answer": "362", "explanation": "361, 400, and 441 are whole numbers multiplied by themselves. 362 lies between 19² and 20².", "sources": ["Derived by integer arithmetic"], "id": "odd-one-out-52", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside Europe in this atlas?", "options": ["Ukraine", "Belarus", "San Marino", "Sierra Leone"], "answer": "Sierra Leone", "explanation": "Sierra Leone is grouped in Africa; the other three are in Europe. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/up.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/bo.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/sm.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/sl.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-53", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside Oceania in this atlas?", "options": ["Solomon Islands", "Samoa", "Burkina Faso", "Papua New Guinea"], "answer": "Burkina Faso", "explanation": "Burkina Faso is grouped in Africa; the other three are in Oceania. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/bp.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/ws.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/uv.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/pp.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-54", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which number is NOT a perfect square?", "options": ["400", "484", "401", "441"], "answer": "401", "explanation": "400, 441, and 484 are whole numbers multiplied by themselves. 401 lies between 20² and 21².", "sources": ["Derived by integer arithmetic"], "id": "odd-one-out-55", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('odd-one-out',11,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside Europe in this atlas?", "options": ["Switzerland", "Belgium", "Ecuador", "Albania"], "answer": "Ecuador", "explanation": "Ecuador is grouped in South America; the other three are in Europe. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/sz.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/be.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/ec.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/al.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-56", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside Europe in this atlas?", "options": ["Ireland", "Mexico", "Latvia", "Czech Republic"], "answer": "Mexico", "explanation": "Mexico is grouped in North America; the other three are in Europe. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ei.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/north-america/mx.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/lg.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ez.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-57", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which number is NOT a perfect square?", "options": ["529", "441", "442", "484"], "answer": "442", "explanation": "441, 484, and 529 are whole numbers multiplied by themselves. 442 lies between 21² and 22².", "sources": ["Derived by integer arithmetic"], "id": "odd-one-out-58", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside South America in this atlas?", "options": ["Brazil", "Uruguay", "Niger", "Venezuela"], "answer": "Niger", "explanation": "Niger is grouped in Africa; the other three are in South America. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/br.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/uy.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ng.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/ve.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-59", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside Europe in this atlas?", "options": ["Hungary", "Romania", "Slovakia", "Tajikistan"], "answer": "Tajikistan", "explanation": "Tajikistan is grouped in Asia; the other three are in Europe. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/hu.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ro.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/lo.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-asia/ti.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-60", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('odd-one-out',12,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which number is NOT a perfect square?", "options": ["576", "529", "485", "484"], "answer": "485", "explanation": "484, 529, and 576 are whole numbers multiplied by themselves. 485 lies between 22² and 23².", "sources": ["Derived by integer arithmetic"], "id": "odd-one-out-61", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside Europe in this atlas?", "options": ["Switzerland", "Romania", "Monaco", "Panama"], "answer": "Panama", "explanation": "Panama is grouped in North America; the other three are in Europe. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/sz.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ro.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/mn.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/pm.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-62", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside South America in this atlas?", "options": ["Belize", "Bolivia", "Uruguay", "Brazil"], "answer": "Belize", "explanation": "Belize is grouped in North America; the other three are in South America. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/bh.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/bl.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/uy.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/br.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-63", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which number is NOT a perfect square?", "options": ["576", "529", "625", "530"], "answer": "530", "explanation": "529, 576, and 625 are whole numbers multiplied by themselves. 530 lies between 23² and 24².", "sources": ["Derived by integer arithmetic"], "id": "odd-one-out-64", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside Europe in this atlas?", "options": ["Portugal", "Hungary", "Luxembourg", "Costa Rica"], "answer": "Costa Rica", "explanation": "Costa Rica is grouped in North America; the other three are in Europe. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/po.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/hu.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/lu.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/cs.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-65", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('odd-one-out',13,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside North America in this atlas?", "options": ["Costa Rica", "Russia", "Saint Kitts and Nevis", "Nicaragua"], "answer": "Russia", "explanation": "Russia is grouped in Europe; the other three are in North America. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/cs.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-asia/rs.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/sc.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/nu.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-66", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which number is NOT a perfect square?", "options": ["625", "676", "577", "576"], "answer": "577", "explanation": "576, 625, and 676 are whole numbers multiplied by themselves. 577 lies between 24² and 25².", "sources": ["Derived by integer arithmetic"], "id": "odd-one-out-67", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside Oceania in this atlas?", "options": ["Papua New Guinea", "Samoa", "Solomon Islands", "Senegal"], "answer": "Senegal", "explanation": "Senegal is grouped in Africa; the other three are in Oceania. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/pp.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/ws.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/bp.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/sg.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-68", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country is outside Africa in this atlas?", "options": ["Botswana", "Guinea-Bissau", "Haiti", "Burkina Faso"], "answer": "Haiti", "explanation": "Haiti is grouped in North America; the other three are in Africa. Classification follows the same atlas as Geography.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/bc.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/pu.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/ha.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/uv.json"], "id": "odd-one-out-69", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which number is NOT a perfect square?", "options": ["729", "625", "626", "676"], "answer": "626", "explanation": "625, 676, and 729 are whole numbers multiplied by themselves. 626 lies between 25² and 26².", "sources": ["Derived by integer arithmetic"], "id": "odd-one-out-70", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',0,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Among the last areas of Sub-Saharan Africa to be drawn into the world economy, its introduction into trade networks around the early 1700s fostered significant competition among its population.\nIts capital is Bangui. Which country is it?", "options": ["Vietnam", "Central African Republic", "Kyrgyzstan", "Palau"], "answer": "Central African Republic", "explanation": "Central African Republic · Bangui. Among the last areas of Sub-Saharan Africa to be drawn into the world economy, its introduction into trade networks around the early 1700s fostered significant competition among its population.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ct.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-1", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "During the second millennium BCE, remnants of this culture fused with the migrating Indo-Aryan peoples.\nIts capital is Islamabad. Which country is it?", "options": ["Pakistan", "Ukraine", "Jamaica", "Kiribati"], "answer": "Pakistan", "explanation": "Pakistan · Islamabad. During the second millennium BCE, remnants of this culture fused with the migrating Indo-Aryan peoples.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-asia/pk.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-2", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "this country was one of three countries that emerged from the collapse of Gran Colombia in 1830, the others being Ecuador and New Granada (Colombia).\nIts capital is Caracas. Which country is it?", "options": ["Guinea", "Venezuela", "Poland", "Tonga"], "answer": "Venezuela", "explanation": "Venezuela · Caracas. Venezuela was one of three countries that emerged from the collapse of Gran Colombia in 1830, the others being Ecuador and New Granada (Colombia).", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/ve.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-3", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "A large portion of present-day this countryn territory became a province of the Russian Empire in 1812 and then unified with Romania in 1918 in the aftermath of World War I.\nIts capital is Chisinau in Romanian (Kishinev in Russian). Which country is it?", "options": ["Moldova", "Bolivia", "Seychelles", "Central African Republic"], "answer": "Moldova", "explanation": "Moldova · Chisinau in Romanian (Kishinev in Russian). A large portion of present-day Moldovan territory became a province of the Russian Empire in 1812 and then unified with Romania in 1918 in the aftermath of World War I.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/md.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-4", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "France ceded possession to Britain in 1763, and this country became a British colony in 1805.\nIts capital is Roseau. Which country is it?", "options": ["Barbados", "Estonia", "Dominica", "Tanzania"], "answer": "Dominica", "explanation": "Dominica · Roseau. France ceded possession to Britain in 1763, and Dominica became a British colony in 1805.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/do.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-5", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',1,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "From the 11th to the 16th centuries, various ethnic groups settled the this country region.\nIts capital is Lome. Which country is it?", "options": ["Bulgaria", "Togo", "Luxembourg", "Mali"], "answer": "Togo", "explanation": "Togo · Lome. From the 11th to the 16th centuries, various ethnic groups settled the Togo region.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/to.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-6", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "After centuries of Danish, Swedish, German, and Russian rule, this country attained independence in 1918.\nIts capital is Tallinn. Which country is it?", "options": ["Honduras", "Republic of the Congo", "Estonia", "Poland"], "answer": "Estonia", "explanation": "Estonia · Tallinn. After centuries of Danish, Swedish, German, and Russian rule, Estonia attained independence in 1918.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/en.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-7", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Upon independence in 1960, the former French region of Middle Congo became the this country.\nIts capital is Brazzaville. Which country is it?", "options": ["Federated States of Micronesia", "Brazil", "Republic of the Congo", "Colombia"], "answer": "Republic of the Congo", "explanation": "Republic of the Congo · Brazzaville. Upon independence in 1960, the former French region of Middle Congo became the Republic of the Congo.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/cf.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-8", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Trade centers such as Mombasa have existed along the this countryn and Tanzanian coastlines, known as the Land of Zanj, since at least the 2nd century.\nIts capital is Nairobi. Which country is it?", "options": ["Angola", "Kenya", "Argentina", "Türkiye"], "answer": "Kenya", "explanation": "Kenya · Nairobi. Trade centers such as Mombasa have existed along the Kenyan and Tanzanian coastlines, known as the Land of Zanj, since at least the 2nd century.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ke.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-9", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The first Austronesian settlers arrived in this country around 1000 BCE, and early this countryns traded and intermarried with Fijian and Tongan nobility.\nIts capital is Apia. Which country is it?", "options": ["Solomon Islands", "Marshall Islands", "Samoa", "United Arab Emirates"], "answer": "Samoa", "explanation": "Samoa · Apia. The first Austronesian settlers arrived in Samoa around 1000 BCE, and early Samoans traded and intermarried with Fijian and Tongan nobility.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/ws.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-10", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',2,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Formerly part of the Ottoman Empire, this country was occupied by the United Kingdom during World War I and was declared a League of Nations mandate under UK administration in 1920.\nIts capital is Baghdad. Which country is it?", "options": ["Samoa", "Bulgaria", "Trinidad and Tobago", "Iraq"], "answer": "Iraq", "explanation": "Iraq · Baghdad. Formerly part of the Ottoman Empire, Iraq was occupied by the United Kingdom during World War I and was declared a League of Nations mandate under UK administration in 1920.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/iz.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-11", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "In the 16th century, Portugal began establishing trading posts along this country’s shoreline.\nIts capital is Bissau. Which country is it?", "options": ["Lesotho", "Nicaragua", "Guinea-Bissau", "Saudi Arabia"], "answer": "Guinea-Bissau", "explanation": "Guinea-Bissau · Bissau. In the 16th century, Portugal began establishing trading posts along Guinea-Bissau’s shoreline.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/pu.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-12", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Modern-day this country has its roots in the ancient Lao kingdom of Lan Xang, established in the 14th century under King FA Ngum.\nIts capital is Vientiane (Viangchan). Which country is it?", "options": ["Zimbabwe", "Laos", "Bahrain", "Azerbaijan"], "answer": "Laos", "explanation": "Laos · Vientiane (Viangchan). Modern-day Laos has its roots in the ancient Lao kingdom of Lan Xang, established in the 14th century under King FA Ngum.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/la.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-13", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Most recently a British colony (since 1814), this country gained its independence in 1964 and declared itself a republic 10 years later.\nIts capital is Valletta. Which country is it?", "options": ["Turkmenistan", "Ivory Coast", "Malta", "United Arab Emirates"], "answer": "Malta", "explanation": "Malta · Valletta. Most recently a British colony (since 1814), Malta gained its independence in 1964 and declared itself a republic 10 years later.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/mt.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-14", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The Dutch abandoned their financially distressed settlement in 1710, although a number of formerly enslaved people remained.\nIts capital is Port Louis. Which country is it?", "options": ["Somalia", "Mauritius", "Jordan", "Bhutan"], "answer": "Mauritius", "explanation": "Mauritius · Port Louis. The Dutch abandoned their financially distressed settlement in 1710, although a number of formerly enslaved people remained.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/mp.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-15", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',3,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The Nile’s annual floods supported agriculture in a desert landscape, helping sustain the kingdoms that built ancient this country’s monuments over thousands of years.\nIts capital is Cairo. Which country is it?", "options": ["Egypt", "San Marino", "Bangladesh", "Tuvalu"], "answer": "Egypt", "explanation": "Egypt · Cairo. The Nile’s annual floods supported agriculture in a desert landscape, helping sustain the kingdoms that built ancient Egypt’s monuments over thousands of years.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/eg.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-16", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Between the 14th and 16th centuries, the Jolof Empire ruled most of this country.\nIts capital is Dakar. Which country is it?", "options": ["Senegal", "Vatican City", "Vietnam", "Russia"], "answer": "Senegal", "explanation": "Senegal · Dakar. Between the 14th and 16th centuries, the Jolof Empire ruled most of Senegal.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/sg.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-17", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "this country became a Christian kingdom in CE 1000 and for many centuries served as a bulwark against Ottoman Turkish expansion in Europe.\nIts capital is Budapest. Which country is it?", "options": ["Bosnia and Herzegovina", "Paraguay", "Georgia", "Hungary"], "answer": "Hungary", "explanation": "Hungary · Budapest. Hungary became a Christian kingdom in CE 1000 and for many centuries served as a bulwark against Ottoman Turkish expansion in Europe.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/hu.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-18", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "European power struggles immersed this country in two devastating world wars in the first half of the 20th century and left the country occupied by the victorious Allied powers of the US, UK, France, and the Soviet Union in 1945.\nIts capital is Berlin. Which country is it?", "options": ["Germany", "Namibia", "Ukraine", "Lithuania"], "answer": "Germany", "explanation": "Germany · Berlin. European power struggles immersed Germany in two devastating world wars in the first half of the 20th century and left the country occupied by the victorious Allied powers of the US, UK, France, and the Soviet Union in 1945.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/gm.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-19", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Celtic tribes arrived in this country between 600 and 150 BCE Norse invasions that began in the late 8th century finally ended when King Brian Boru defeated the Danes in 1014.\nIts capital is Dublin. Which country is it?", "options": ["Vatican City", "Bahrain", "India", "Ireland"], "answer": "Ireland", "explanation": "Ireland · Dublin. Celtic tribes arrived in Ireland between 600 and 150 BCE Norse invasions that began in the late 8th century finally ended when King Brian Boru defeated the Danes in 1014.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ei.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-20", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',4,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Two centuries of Viking raids into Europe tapered off after King Olav Tryggvason adopted Christianity in 994; conversion of the Norwegian kingdom occurred over the next several decades.\nIts capital is Oslo. Which country is it?", "options": ["Norway", "Kuwait", "Slovenia", "Panama"], "answer": "Norway", "explanation": "Norway · Oslo. Two centuries of Viking raids into Europe tapered off after King Olav Tryggvason adopted Christianity in 994; conversion of the Norwegian kingdom occurred over the next several decades.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/no.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-21", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The Tajik people came under Russian imperial rule in the 1860s and 1870s, but Russia''s hold on Central Asia weakened following the Revolution of 1917.\nIts capital is Dushanbe. Which country is it?", "options": ["Tajikistan", "Brunei", "Guyana", "Bahrain"], "answer": "Tajikistan", "explanation": "Tajikistan · Dushanbe. The Tajik people came under Russian imperial rule in the 1860s and 1870s, but Russia''s hold on Central Asia weakened following the Revolution of 1917.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-asia/ti.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-22", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Russia conquered and united the disparate territories of present-day this country in the late 19th century.\nIts capital is Tashkent (Toshkent). Which country is it?", "options": ["Zimbabwe", "Uzbekistan", "Liechtenstein", "Malta"], "answer": "Uzbekistan", "explanation": "Uzbekistan · Tashkent (Toshkent). Russia conquered and united the disparate territories of present-day Uzbekistan in the late 19th century.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-asia/uz.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-23", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The Genoese built a fortress on the site of present-day this country in 1215.\nIts capital is Monaco. Which country is it?", "options": ["Portugal", "Monaco", "Eswatini", "Somalia"], "answer": "Monaco", "explanation": "Monaco · Monaco. The Genoese built a fortress on the site of present-day Monaco in 1215.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/mn.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-24", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The Trucial States of the Persian Gulf coast granted the UK control of their defense and foreign affairs in 19th-century treaties.\nIts capital is Abu Dhabi. Which country is it?", "options": ["Germany", "Uzbekistan", "United Arab Emirates", "Rwanda"], "answer": "United Arab Emirates", "explanation": "United Arab Emirates · Abu Dhabi. The Trucial States of the Persian Gulf coast granted the UK control of their defense and foreign affairs in 19th-century treaties.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/ae.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-25", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',5,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The region of present-day this country once contained the ancient kingdoms of Colchis (known as Egrisi locally) and Kartli-Iberia.\nIts capital is Tbilisi. Which country is it?", "options": ["Nepal", "Georgia", "Panama", "Greece"], "answer": "Georgia", "explanation": "Georgia · Tbilisi. The region of present-day Georgia once contained the ancient kingdoms of Colchis (known as Egrisi locally) and Kartli-Iberia.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-asia/gg.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-26", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Carib Indians occupied the islands of the West Indies for hundreds of years before the British and French began settlement in 1623.\nIts capital is Basseterre. Which country is it?", "options": ["Saint Kitts and Nevis", "Philippines", "Libya", "Rwanda"], "answer": "Saint Kitts and Nevis", "explanation": "Saint Kitts and Nevis · Basseterre. Carib Indians occupied the islands of the West Indies for hundreds of years before the British and French began settlement in 1623.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/sc.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-27", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country has Suva (on Viti Levu) as its capital?", "options": ["Fiji", "Brunei", "Guinea-Bissau", "Seychelles"], "answer": "Fiji", "explanation": "Fiji · Suva (on Viti Levu). Austronesians settled Fiji around 1000 BCE, followed by successive waves of Melanesians starting around the first century CE Fijians traded with Polynesian groups in Samoa and Tonga, and by about 900, much of Fiji was in the Tu’i Tongan Empire’s sphere of influence.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/fj.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-28", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Early Spanish and French settlements were succeeded by an English colony in 1667.\nIts capital is Saint John''s. Which country is it?", "options": ["Iraq", "Liberia", "Antigua and Barbuda", "The Bahamas"], "answer": "Antigua and Barbuda", "explanation": "Antigua and Barbuda · Saint John''s. Early Spanish and French settlements were succeeded by an English colony in 1667.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/ac.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-29", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "After declaring independence from the Ottoman Empire in 1912, this country experienced a period of political upheaval that led to a short-lived monarchy, which ended in 1939 when Italy conquered the country.\nIts capital is Tirana (Tirane). Which country is it?", "options": ["Mauritius", "Ukraine", "Bulgaria", "Albania"], "answer": "Albania", "explanation": "Albania · Tirana (Tirane). After declaring independence from the Ottoman Empire in 1912, Albania experienced a period of political upheaval that led to a short-lived monarchy, which ended in 1939 when Italy conquered the country.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/al.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-30", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',6,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "At the close of World War I, the Czechs and Slovaks of the former Austro-Hungarian Empire merged to form Czechoslovakia, a parliamentarian democracy.\nIts capital is Prague. Which country is it?", "options": ["Eswatini", "Nigeria", "Dominica", "Czech Republic"], "answer": "Czech Republic", "explanation": "Czech Republic · Prague. At the close of World War I, the Czechs and Slovaks of the former Austro-Hungarian Empire merged to form Czechoslovakia, a parliamentarian democracy.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ez.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-31", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "By the 5th century CE, Kogoryo emerged as the most powerful, with control over much of the Peninsula and part of Manchuria (modern-day northeast China).\nIts capital is Seoul. Which country is it?", "options": ["Andorra", "Algeria", "Thailand", "South Korea"], "answer": "South Korea", "explanation": "South Korea · Seoul. By the 5th century CE, Kogoryo emerged as the most powerful, with control over much of the Peninsula and part of Manchuria (modern-day northeast China).", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/ks.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-32", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The principalities of Wallachia and Moldavia -- for centuries under the control of the Turkish Ottoman Empire -- secured their autonomy through the Treaty of Paris in 1856.\nIts capital is Bucharest. Which country is it?", "options": ["Croatia", "Romania", "Hungary", "Uruguay"], "answer": "Romania", "explanation": "Romania · Bucharest. The principalities of Wallachia and Moldavia -- for centuries under the control of the Turkish Ottoman Empire -- secured their autonomy through the Treaty of Paris in 1856.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ro.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-33", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Berbers have inhabited central north Africa since ancient times, but Phoenicians, Greeks, Carthaginians, Persians, Egyptians, Romans, and Vandals have all settled and ruled the region.\nIts capital is Tripoli (Tarabulus). Which country is it?", "options": ["Central African Republic", "Philippines", "Libya", "Federated States of Micronesia"], "answer": "Libya", "explanation": "Libya · Tripoli (Tarabulus). Berbers have inhabited central north Africa since ancient times, but Phoenicians, Greeks, Carthaginians, Persians, Egyptians, Romans, and Vandals have all settled and ruled the region.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ly.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-34", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "By 1000 BCE, Micronesian and Polynesian settlers inhabited this country, and the island was divided among 12 clans.\nIts capital is no official capital; government offices in the Yaren District. Which country is it?", "options": ["Canada", "Nicaragua", "Nauru", "Nigeria"], "answer": "Nauru", "explanation": "Nauru · no official capital; government offices in the Yaren District. By 1000 BCE, Micronesian and Polynesian settlers inhabited Nauru, and the island was divided among 12 clans.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/nr.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-35", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',7,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The island of Timor was actively involved in Southeast Asian trading networks for centuries, and by the 14th century, it exported sandalwood, slaves, honey, and wax.\nIts capital is Dili. Which country is it?", "options": ["Niger", "East Timor", "Burkina Faso", "Egypt"], "answer": "East Timor", "explanation": "East Timor · Dili. The island of Timor was actively involved in Southeast Asian trading networks for centuries, and by the 14th century, it exported sandalwood, slaves, honey, and wax.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/tt.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-36", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The Taureg kingdom of Takedda was one of the largest kingdoms in the north and played a prominent role in regional trade in the 14th century.\nIts capital is Niamey. Which country is it?", "options": ["Ukraine", "Mozambique", "Ivory Coast", "Niger"], "answer": "Niger", "explanation": "Niger · Niamey. The Taureg kingdom of Takedda was one of the largest kingdoms in the north and played a prominent role in regional trade in the 14th century.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ng.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-37", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "A sultanate since the 12th century, the this country became a British protectorate in 1887 and a republic in 1968, three years after independence.\nIts capital is Malé. Which country is it?", "options": ["Maldives", "Czech Republic", "Barbados", "Dominica"], "answer": "Maldives", "explanation": "Maldives · Malé. A sultanate since the 12th century, the Maldives became a British protectorate in 1887 and a republic in 1968, three years after independence.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-asia/mv.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-38", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "this country won independence from the Ottoman Empire in 1830 and became a kingdom.\nIts capital is Athens. Which country is it?", "options": ["Greece", "Belgium", "Malawi", "Gabon"], "answer": "Greece", "explanation": "Greece · Athens. Greece won independence from the Ottoman Empire in 1830 and became a kingdom.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/gr.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-39", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "After more than three centuries under Portuguese rule, this country gained its independence in 1822, maintaining a monarchical system of government until the abolition of slavery in 1888 and the subsequent proclamation of a republic by the military in 1889.\nIts capital is Brasília. Which country is it?", "options": ["Brazil", "Gabon", "Saudi Arabia", "Serbia"], "answer": "Brazil", "explanation": "Brazil · Brasília. After more than three centuries under Portuguese rule, Brazil gained its independence in 1822, maintaining a monarchical system of government until the abolition of slavery in 1888 and the subsequent proclamation of a republic by the military in 1889.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/br.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-40", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',8,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The first Austronesian voyagers arrived in the Gilbert Islands as early as 3000 BCE, but these islands were not widely settled until about CE 200 by Micronesians.\nIts capital is Tarawa. Which country is it?", "options": ["Uzbekistan", "Saint Kitts and Nevis", "South Korea", "Kiribati"], "answer": "Kiribati", "explanation": "Kiribati · Tarawa. The first Austronesian voyagers arrived in the Gilbert Islands as early as 3000 BCE, but these islands were not widely settled until about CE 200 by Micronesians.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/kr.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-41", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The Kingdom of this country (colloquially known as North this country) became independent from the Ottoman Empire in 1918 and in 1962 became the this country Arab Republic.\nIts capital is Sanaa. Which country is it?", "options": ["Yemen", "India", "North Korea", "Djibouti"], "answer": "Yemen", "explanation": "Yemen · Sanaa. The Kingdom of Yemen (colloquially known as North Yemen) became independent from the Ottoman Empire in 1918 and in 1962 became the Yemen Arab Republic.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/ym.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-42", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "German colonial rule in the late 19th and early 20th centuries and Belgian rule after World War I preserved this country’s monarchy.\nIts capital is Gitega (political capital), Bujumbura (commercial capital). Which country is it?", "options": ["Peru", "Burundi", "Antigua and Barbuda", "Honduras"], "answer": "Burundi", "explanation": "Burundi · Gitega (political capital), Bujumbura (commercial capital). German colonial rule in the late 19th and early 20th centuries and Belgian rule after World War I preserved Burundi’s monarchy.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/by.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-43", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "A former British colony, this country became independent in 1960 after years of resistance to British rule.\nIts capital is Nicosia (Lefkosia/Lefkosa). Which country is it?", "options": ["Cyprus", "Switzerland", "Federated States of Micronesia", "North Macedonia"], "answer": "Cyprus", "explanation": "Cyprus · Nicosia (Lefkosia/Lefkosa). A former British colony, Cyprus became independent in 1960 after years of resistance to British rule.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/cy.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-44", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The Tokugawa shogunate, a hereditary military government, began in 1603 after decades of civil war. More than two centuries of relative stability helped this countryese arts and urban culture flourish.\nIts capital is Tokyo. Which country is it?", "options": ["Panama", "Dominica", "Japan", "Luxembourg"], "answer": "Japan", "explanation": "Japan · Tokyo. The Tokugawa shogunate, a hereditary military government, began in 1603 after decades of civil war. More than two centuries of relative stability helped Japanese arts and urban culture flourish.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/ja.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-45", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',9,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Dutch traders landed at the southern tip of present-day this country in 1652 and established a stopover point on the spice route between the Netherlands and the Far East, founding the city of Cape Town.\nIts capital is Pretoria (administrative capital); Cape Town (legislative capital); Bloemfontein (judicial capital). Which country is it?", "options": ["Seychelles", "Yemen", "Djibouti", "South Africa"], "answer": "South Africa", "explanation": "South Africa · Pretoria (administrative capital); Cape Town (legislative capital); Bloemfontein (judicial capital). Dutch traders landed at the southern tip of present-day South Africa in 1652 and established a stopover point on the spice route between the Netherlands and the Far East, founding the city of Cape Town.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/sf.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-46", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "this country''s powerful world empire of the 16th and 17th centuries ultimately yielded command of the seas to England.\nIts capital is Madrid. Which country is it?", "options": ["Madagascar", "Pakistan", "Brunei", "Spain"], "answer": "Spain", "explanation": "Spain · Madrid. Spain''s powerful world empire of the 16th and 17th centuries ultimately yielded command of the seas to England.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/sp.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-47", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "In 1816, the United Provinces of the Río de la Plata declared their independence from Spain.\nIts capital is Buenos Aires. Which country is it?", "options": ["Marshall Islands", "Eswatini", "Dominica", "Argentina"], "answer": "Argentina", "explanation": "Argentina · Buenos Aires. In 1816, the United Provinces of the Río de la Plata declared their independence from Spain.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/ar.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-48", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "this country traces its founding to Marinus, a Christian stonemason said to have established a community in 301 CE. This is a founding tradition, rather than a securely documented date.\nIts capital is San Marino (city). Which country is it?", "options": ["Jordan", "Mauritania", "San Marino", "Moldova"], "answer": "San Marino", "explanation": "San Marino · San Marino (city). San Marino traces its founding to Marinus, a Christian stonemason said to have established a community in 301 CE. This is a founding tradition, rather than a securely documented date.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/sm.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-49", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "A global maritime power during the 15th and 16th centuries, this country lost much of its wealth and status with the destruction of Lisbon in a 1755 earthquake, occupation during the Napoleonic Wars, and the independence of Brazil, its wealthiest colony, in 1822.\nIts capital is Lisbon. Which country is it?", "options": ["Portugal", "Maldives", "Burundi", "Honduras"], "answer": "Portugal", "explanation": "Portugal · Lisbon. A global maritime power during the 15th and 16th centuries, Portugal lost much of its wealth and status with the destruction of Lisbon in a 1755 earthquake, occupation during the Napoleonic Wars, and the independence of Brazil, its wealthiest colony, in 1822.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/po.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-50", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',10,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "After Britain’s victory in the 1865 Duar War, Britain and this country signed the Treaty of Sinchulu, under which this country would receive an annual subsidy in exchange for ceding land to British India.\nIts capital is Thimphu. Which country is it?", "options": ["Portugal", "Algeria", "Nigeria", "Bhutan"], "answer": "Bhutan", "explanation": "Bhutan · Thimphu. After Britain’s victory in the 1865 Duar War, Britain and Bhutan signed the Treaty of Sinchulu, under which Bhutan would receive an annual subsidy in exchange for ceding land to British India.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-asia/bt.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-51", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "After Iraq invaded Kuwait in 1990, this country took in the Kuwaiti royal family and 400,000 refugees, while allowing Western and Arab troops to deploy on its soil and liberate Kuwait the following year.\nIts capital is Riyadh. Which country is it?", "options": ["Antigua and Barbuda", "Zambia", "Saudi Arabia", "Montenegro"], "answer": "Saudi Arabia", "explanation": "Saudi Arabia · Riyadh. After Iraq invaded Kuwait in 1990, Saudi Arabia took in the Kuwaiti royal family and 400,000 refugees, while allowing Western and Arab troops to deploy on its soil and liberate Kuwait the following year.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/sa.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-52", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The first Sinhalese arrived in this country late in the 6th century BCE, probably from northern India.\nIts capital is Colombo (commercial capital); Sri Jayewardenepura Kotte (legislative capital). Which country is it?", "options": ["Panama", "Afghanistan", "El Salvador", "Sri Lanka"], "answer": "Sri Lanka", "explanation": "Sri Lanka · Colombo (commercial capital); Sri Jayewardenepura Kotte (legislative capital). The first Sinhalese arrived in Sri Lanka late in the 6th century BCE, probably from northern India.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-asia/ce.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-53", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "In 1918, the Croats, Serbs, and Slovenes formed a kingdom known after 1929 as Yugoslavia.\nIts capital is Belgrade (Beograd). Which country is it?", "options": ["Serbia", "Qatar", "Croatia", "South Africa"], "answer": "Serbia", "explanation": "Serbia · Belgrade (Beograd). In 1918, the Croats, Serbs, and Slovenes formed a kingdom known after 1929 as Yugoslavia.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ri.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-54", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country has Dhaka as its capital?", "options": ["Bangladesh", "Thailand", "Montenegro", "Russia"], "answer": "Bangladesh", "explanation": "Bangladesh · Dhaka. The huge delta region at the confluence of the Ganges and Brahmaputra River systems -- now referred to as Bangladesh -- was a loosely incorporated outpost of various empires for much of the first millennium CE Muslim conversions and settlement in the region began in the 10th century, primarily from Arab and Persian traders and preachers.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-asia/bg.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-55", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',11,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "By the 5th century CE, Kogoryo emerged as the most powerful, with control over much of the Peninsula and part of Manchuria (modern-day northeast China).\nIts capital is Pyongyang. Which country is it?", "options": ["North Korea", "East Timor", "Singapore", "Tajikistan"], "answer": "North Korea", "explanation": "North Korea · Pyongyang. By the 5th century CE, Kogoryo emerged as the most powerful, with control over much of the Peninsula and part of Manchuria (modern-day northeast China).", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/kn.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-56", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The remainder of this country’s ethnic groups derive from Sub-Saharan ethnic groups originating mainly from the Senegal River Valley, including descendants of former enslaved peoples.\nIts capital is Nouakchott. Which country is it?", "options": ["Sweden", "Nauru", "Mauritania", "Japan"], "answer": "Mauritania", "explanation": "Mauritania · Nouakchott. The remainder of Mauritania’s ethnic groups derive from Sub-Saharan ethnic groups originating mainly from the Senegal River Valley, including descendants of former enslaved peoples.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/mr.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-57", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "this country''s early history included periods of occupation by outside forces and eventual power consolidation under this countryese dynastic families.\nIts capital is Hanoi (Ha Noi). Which country is it?", "options": ["Nauru", "Chad", "Vietnam", "Uganda"], "answer": "Vietnam", "explanation": "Vietnam · Hanoi (Ha Noi). Vietnam''s early history included periods of occupation by outside forces and eventual power consolidation under Vietnamese dynastic families.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/vm.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-58", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Which country has Castries as its capital?", "options": ["The Gambia", "Zambia", "Colombia", "Saint Lucia"], "answer": "Saint Lucia", "explanation": "Saint Lucia · Castries. England and France contested Saint Lucia -- with its fine natural harbor at Castries and burgeoning sugar industry -- throughout the 17th and early 18th centuries, with possession changing 14 times; it was finally ceded to the UK in 1814 and became part of the British Windward Islands colony.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/st.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-59", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Bantu-speaking people settled in the area now called this country in 6th century CE; by the 10th century various Bantu groups had established kingdoms, of which Kongo became the most powerful.\nIts capital is Luanda. Which country is it?", "options": ["Japan", "Angola", "Palau", "Chad"], "answer": "Angola", "explanation": "Angola · Luanda. Bantu-speaking people settled in the area now called Angola in 6th century CE; by the 10th century various Bantu groups had established kingdoms, of which Kongo became the most powerful.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ao.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-60", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',12,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The Kingdom of Dahomey emerged on the Abomey plateau in the 17th century and was a regional power for much of the 18th and 19th centuries.\nIts capital is Porto-Novo (constitutional capital); Cotonou (seat of government). Which country is it?", "options": ["North Korea", "Zimbabwe", "South Korea", "Benin"], "answer": "Benin", "explanation": "Benin · Porto-Novo (constitutional capital); Cotonou (seat of government). The Kingdom of Dahomey emerged on the Abomey plateau in the 17th century and was a regional power for much of the 18th and 19th centuries.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/bn.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-61", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "this country traces its roots to the 9th century state of Great Moravia.\nIts capital is Bratislava. Which country is it?", "options": ["East Timor", "Angola", "El Salvador", "Slovakia"], "answer": "Slovakia", "explanation": "Slovakia · Bratislava. Slovakia traces its roots to the 9th century state of Great Moravia.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/lo.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-62", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "An ancient crossroads for various migrations, this country has as many as 65 ethnic groups that speak languages from three of Africa’s four major linguistic families.\nIts capital is Kampala. Which country is it?", "options": ["Uganda", "Oman", "Sri Lanka", "Bahrain"], "answer": "Uganda", "explanation": "Uganda · Kampala. An ancient crossroads for various migrations, Uganda has as many as 65 ethnic groups that speak languages from three of Africa’s four major linguistic families.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ug.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-63", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The French settled this country in the 17th century, established sugar estates, and imported large numbers of African slaves.\nIts capital is Saint George''s. Which country is it?", "options": ["São Tomé and Príncipe", "Saint Lucia", "Japan", "Grenada"], "answer": "Grenada", "explanation": "Grenada · Saint George''s. The French settled Grenada in the 17th century, established sugar estates, and imported large numbers of African slaves.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/gj.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-64", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "The Bulgars, a Central Asian Turkic tribe, merged with the local Slavic inhabitants in the late 7th century to form the first this countryn state.\nIts capital is Sofia. Which country is it?", "options": ["Bulgaria", "Panama", "Saudi Arabia", "Suriname"], "answer": "Bulgaria", "explanation": "Bulgaria · Sofia. The Bulgars, a Central Asian Turkic tribe, merged with the local Slavic inhabitants in the late 7th century to form the first Bulgarian state.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/bu.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-65", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('passport-puzzle',13,1,'[{"kind": "choice", "prompt": "In the 10th century, Muslim merchants established some of this country’s earliest large settlements as trans-Saharan trade hubs.\nIts capital is Banjul. Which country is it?", "options": ["Solomon Islands", "Kenya", "The Gambia", "South Sudan"], "answer": "The Gambia", "explanation": "The Gambia · Banjul. In the 10th century, Muslim merchants established some of The Gambia’s earliest large settlements as trans-Saharan trade hubs.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ga.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-66", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Founded in the 12th century, the Principality of Muscovy emerged from over 200 years of Mongol domination (13th-15th centuries) and gradually conquered and absorbed surrounding principalities.\nIts capital is Moscow. Which country is it?", "options": ["Russia", "Honduras", "Central African Republic", "Thailand"], "answer": "Russia", "explanation": "Russia · Moscow. Founded in the 12th century, the Principality of Muscovy emerged from over 200 years of Mongol domination (13th-15th centuries) and gradually conquered and absorbed surrounding principalities.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-asia/rs.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-67", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Between CE 800 and 1100, immigrant Muslim Arabs and Persians set up coastal trading posts along the Gulf of Aden and the Indian Ocean, solidifying present-day this country’s close trading relationship with the Arab Peninsula.\nIts capital is Mogadishu. Which country is it?", "options": ["Sierra Leone", "Portugal", "San Marino", "Somalia"], "answer": "Somalia", "explanation": "Somalia · Mogadishu. Between CE 800 and 1100, immigrant Muslim Arabs and Persians set up coastal trading posts along the Gulf of Aden and the Indian Ocean, solidifying present-day Somalia’s close trading relationship with the Arab Peninsula.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/so.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-68", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Humans arrived in the this country in the first millennium BCE and gradually created permanent settlements on the various atolls.\nIts capital is Majuro. Which country is it?", "options": ["Slovenia", "Senegal", "Marshall Islands", "Mauritania"], "answer": "Marshall Islands", "explanation": "Marshall Islands · Majuro. Humans arrived in the Marshall Islands in the first millennium BCE and gradually created permanent settlements on the various atolls.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/rm.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-69", "version": 1}, {"kind": "choice", "prompt": "Settled by Norwegian and Celtic (Scottish and Irish) immigrants during the late 9th and 10th centuries CE, this country boasts the world''s oldest functioning legislative assembly, the Althingi, which was established in 930.\nIts capital is Reykjavik. Which country is it?", "options": ["Iceland", "Trinidad and Tobago", "Pakistan", "Saudi Arabia"], "answer": "Iceland", "explanation": "Iceland · Reykjavik. Settled by Norwegian and Celtic (Scottish and Irish) immigrants during the late 9th and 10th centuries CE, Iceland boasts the world''s oldest functioning legislative assembly, the Althingi, which was established in 930.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ic.json"], "id": "passport-puzzle-70", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',0,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Middle Africa.", "Landscape: vast, flat to rolling plateau; scattered hills in northeast and southwest.", "Capital: Bangui.", "The name begins with Ce and has 24 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Central African Republic", "aliases": ["Central African Republic"], "explanation": "Among the last areas of Sub-Saharan Africa to be drawn into the world economy, its introduction into trade networks around the early 1700s fostered significant competition among its population.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ct.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-1", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Asia.", "Landscape: divided into three major geographic areas: the northern highlands, the Indus River plain in the center and east, and the Balochistan Plateau in the south and west.", "Capital: Islamabad.", "The name begins with Pa and has 8 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Pakistan", "aliases": ["Pakistan", "Islamic Republic of Pakistan"], "explanation": "During the second millennium BCE, remnants of this culture fused with the migrating Indo-Aryan peoples.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-asia/pk.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-2", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: South America.", "Landscape: Andes Mountains and Maracaibo Lowlands in northwest; central plains (llanos); Guiana Highlands in southeast.", "Capital: Caracas.", "The name begins with Ve and has 9 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Venezuela", "aliases": ["Venezuela", "Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela"], "explanation": "Venezuela was one of three countries that emerged from the collapse of Gran Colombia in 1830, the others being Ecuador and New Granada (Colombia).", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/ve.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-3", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Europe.", "Landscape: rolling steppe, gradual slope south to Black Sea.", "Capital: Chisinau in Romanian (Kishinev in Russian).", "The name begins with Mo and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Moldova", "aliases": ["Moldova", "Republic of Moldova"], "explanation": "A large portion of present-day Moldovan territory became a province of the Russian Empire in 1812 and then unified with Romania in 1918 in the aftermath of World War I.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/md.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-4", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Caribbean.", "Landscape: rugged mountains of volcanic origin.", "Capital: Roseau.", "The name begins with Do and has 8 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Dominica", "aliases": ["Dominica", "Commonwealth of Dominica"], "explanation": "France ceded possession to Britain in 1763, and Dominica became a British colony in 1805.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/do.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-5", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',1,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Africa.", "Landscape: gently rolling savanna in north; central hills; southern plateau; low coastal plain with extensive lagoons and marshes.", "Capital: Lome.", "The name begins with To and has 4 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Togo", "aliases": ["Togo", "Togolese Republic"], "explanation": "From the 11th to the 16th centuries, various ethnic groups settled the Togo region.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/to.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-6", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Northern Europe.", "Landscape: marshy, lowlands; flat in the north, hilly in the south.", "Capital: Tallinn.", "The name begins with Es and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Estonia", "aliases": ["Estonia", "Republic of Estonia"], "explanation": "After centuries of Danish, Swedish, German, and Russian rule, Estonia attained independence in 1918.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/en.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-7", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Middle Africa.", "Landscape: coastal plain, southern basin, central plateau, northern basin.", "Capital: Brazzaville.", "The name begins with Re and has 21 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Republic of the Congo", "aliases": ["Republic of the Congo", "Congo Brazzaville"], "explanation": "Upon independence in 1960, the former French region of Middle Congo became the Republic of the Congo.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/cf.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-8", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Africa.", "Landscape: low plains rise to central highlands bisected by Great Rift Valley; fertile plateau in west.", "Capital: Nairobi.", "The name begins with Ke and has 5 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Kenya", "aliases": ["Kenya", "Republic of Kenya"], "explanation": "Trade centers such as Mombasa have existed along the Kenyan and Tanzanian coastlines, known as the Land of Zanj, since at least the 2nd century.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ke.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-9", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Polynesia.", "Landscape: two main islands (Savaii, Upolu) and several smaller islands and uninhabited islets; narrow coastal plain with volcanic, rugged mountains in interior.", "Capital: Apia.", "The name begins with Sa and has 5 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Samoa", "aliases": ["Samoa", "Independent State of Samoa"], "explanation": "The first Austronesian settlers arrived in Samoa around 1000 BCE, and early Samoans traded and intermarried with Fijian and Tongan nobility.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/ws.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-10", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',2,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Asia.", "Landscape: mostly broad plains; reedy marshes along Iranian border in south with large flooded areas; mountains along borders with Iran and Turkey.", "Capital: Baghdad.", "The name begins with Ir and has 4 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Iraq", "aliases": ["Iraq", "Republic of Iraq"], "explanation": "Formerly part of the Ottoman Empire, Iraq was occupied by the United Kingdom during World War I and was declared a League of Nations mandate under UK administration in 1920.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/iz.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-11", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Africa.", "Landscape: mostly low-lying coastal plain with a deeply indented estuarine coastline rising to savanna in east; numerous off-shore islands including the Arquipelago Dos Bijagos consisting of 18 main islands and many small islets.", "Capital: Bissau.", "The name begins with Gu and has 13 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Guinea-Bissau", "aliases": ["Guinea-Bissau", "Republic of Guinea-Bissau"], "explanation": "In the 16th century, Portugal began establishing trading posts along Guinea-Bissau’s shoreline.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/pu.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-12", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: South-Eastern Asia.", "Landscape: mostly rugged mountains; some plains and plateaus.", "Capital: Vientiane (Viangchan).", "The name begins with La and has 4 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Laos", "aliases": ["Laos", "Lao PDR", "Lao People''s Democratic Republic"], "explanation": "Modern-day Laos has its roots in the ancient Lao kingdom of Lan Xang, established in the 14th century under King FA Ngum.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/la.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-13", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Europe.", "Landscape: mostly low, rocky, flat to dissected plains; many coastal cliffs.", "Capital: Valletta.", "The name begins with Ma and has 5 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Malta", "aliases": ["Malta", "Republic of Malta"], "explanation": "Most recently a British colony (since 1814), Malta gained its independence in 1964 and declared itself a republic 10 years later.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/mt.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-14", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Africa.", "Landscape: small coastal plain rising to discontinuous mountains encircling central plateau.", "Capital: Port Louis.", "The name begins with Ma and has 9 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Mauritius", "aliases": ["Mauritius", "Republic of Mauritius"], "explanation": "The Dutch abandoned their financially distressed settlement in 1710, although a number of formerly enslaved people remained.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/mp.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-15", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',3,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Northern Africa.", "Landscape: vast desert plateau interrupted by Nile valley and delta.", "Capital: Cairo.", "The name begins with Eg and has 5 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Egypt", "aliases": ["Egypt", "Arab Republic of Egypt"], "explanation": "The Nile’s annual floods supported agriculture in a desert landscape, helping sustain the kingdoms that built ancient Egypt’s monuments over thousands of years.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/eg.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-16", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Africa.", "Landscape: generally low, rolling, plains rising to foothills in southeast.", "Capital: Dakar.", "The name begins with Se and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Senegal", "aliases": ["Senegal", "Republic of Senegal"], "explanation": "Between the 14th and 16th centuries, the Jolof Empire ruled most of Senegal.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/sg.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-17", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Europe.", "Landscape: mostly flat to rolling plains; hills and low mountains on the Slovakian border.", "Capital: Budapest.", "The name begins with Hu and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Hungary", "aliases": ["Hungary", "Republic of Hungary"], "explanation": "Hungary became a Christian kingdom in CE 1000 and for many centuries served as a bulwark against Ottoman Turkish expansion in Europe.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/hu.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-18", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Europe.", "Landscape: lowlands in north, uplands in center, Bavarian Alps in south.", "Capital: Berlin.", "The name begins with Ge and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Germany", "aliases": ["Germany", "Federal Republic of Germany"], "explanation": "European power struggles immersed Germany in two devastating world wars in the first half of the 20th century and left the country occupied by the victorious Allied powers of the US, UK, France, and the Soviet Union in 1945.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/gm.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-19", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Northern Europe.", "Landscape: mostly flat to rolling interior plain surrounded by rugged hills and low mountains; sea cliffs on west coast.", "Capital: Dublin.", "The name begins with Ir and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Ireland", "aliases": ["Ireland"], "explanation": "Celtic tribes arrived in Ireland between 600 and 150 BCE Norse invasions that began in the late 8th century finally ended when King Brian Boru defeated the Danes in 1014.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ei.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-20", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',4,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Northern Europe.", "Landscape: glaciated; mostly high plateaus and rugged mountains broken by fertile valleys; small, scattered plains; coastline deeply indented by fjords; arctic tundra in north.", "Capital: Oslo.", "The name begins with No and has 6 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Norway", "aliases": ["Norway", "Kingdom of Norway"], "explanation": "Two centuries of Viking raids into Europe tapered off after King Olav Tryggvason adopted Christianity in 994; conversion of the Norwegian kingdom occurred over the next several decades.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/no.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-21", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Central Asia.", "Landscape: mountainous region dominated by the Alay Mountains in the north and the Pamirs in the southeast; western Fergana Valley in north, Kofirnihon and Vakhsh Valleys in southwest.", "Capital: Dushanbe.", "The name begins with Ta and has 10 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Tajikistan", "aliases": ["Tajikistan", "Republic of Tajikistan"], "explanation": "The Tajik people came under Russian imperial rule in the 1860s and 1870s, but Russia''s hold on Central Asia weakened following the Revolution of 1917.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-asia/ti.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-22", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Central Asia.", "Landscape: mostly flat-to-rolling sandy desert with dunes; broad, flat intensely irrigated river valleys along course of Amu Darya, Syr Darya (Sirdaryo), and Zaravshan; Fergana Valley in east surrounded by mountainous Tajikistan and Kyrgyzstan; shrinking Aral Sea in west.", "Capital: Tashkent (Toshkent).", "The name begins with Uz and has 10 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Uzbekistan", "aliases": ["Uzbekistan", "Republic of Uzbekistan"], "explanation": "Russia conquered and united the disparate territories of present-day Uzbekistan in the late 19th century.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-asia/uz.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-23", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Europe.", "Landscape: hilly, rugged, rocky.", "Capital: Monaco.", "The name begins with Mo and has 6 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Monaco", "aliases": ["Monaco", "Principality of Monaco"], "explanation": "The Genoese built a fortress on the site of present-day Monaco in 1215.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/mn.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-24", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Asia.", "Landscape: flat, barren coastal plain merging into rolling sand dunes of vast desert; mountains in east.", "Capital: Abu Dhabi.", "The name begins with Un and has 20 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "United Arab Emirates", "aliases": ["United Arab Emirates"], "explanation": "The Trucial States of the Persian Gulf coast granted the UK control of their defense and foreign affairs in 19th-century treaties.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/ae.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-25", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',5,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Asia.", "Landscape: largely mountainous with Great Caucasus Mountains in the north and Lesser Caucasus Mountains in the south; Kolkhet''is Dablobi (Kolkhida Lowland) opens to the Black Sea in the west; Mtkvari River Basin in the east; fertile soils in river valley flood plains and foothills of Kolkhida Lowland.", "Capital: Tbilisi.", "The name begins with Ge and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Georgia", "aliases": ["Georgia"], "explanation": "The region of present-day Georgia once contained the ancient kingdoms of Colchis (known as Egrisi locally) and Kartli-Iberia.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-asia/gg.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-26", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Caribbean.", "Landscape: volcanic with mountainous interiors.", "Capital: Basseterre.", "The name begins with Sa and has 21 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Saint Kitts and Nevis", "aliases": ["Saint Kitts and Nevis", "Federation of Saint Kitts and Nevis"], "explanation": "Carib Indians occupied the islands of the West Indies for hundreds of years before the British and French began settlement in 1623.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/sc.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-27", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Melanesia.", "Landscape: mostly mountains of volcanic origin.", "Capital: Suva (on Viti Levu).", "The name begins with Fi and has 4 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Fiji", "aliases": ["Fiji", "Republic of Fiji"], "explanation": "Austronesians settled Fiji around 1000 BCE, followed by successive waves of Melanesians starting around the first century CE Fijians traded with Polynesian groups in Samoa and Tonga, and by about 900, much of Fiji was in the Tu’i Tongan Empire’s sphere of influence.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/fj.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-28", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Caribbean.", "Landscape: mostly low-lying limestone and coral islands, with some higher volcanic areas.", "Capital: Saint John''s.", "The name begins with An and has 19 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Antigua and Barbuda", "aliases": ["Antigua and Barbuda"], "explanation": "Early Spanish and French settlements were succeeded by an English colony in 1667.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/ac.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-29", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Europe.", "Landscape: mostly mountains and hills; small plains along coast.", "Capital: Tirana (Tirane).", "The name begins with Al and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Albania", "aliases": ["Albania", "Republic of Albania"], "explanation": "After declaring independence from the Ottoman Empire in 1912, Albania experienced a period of political upheaval that led to a short-lived monarchy, which ended in 1939 when Italy conquered the country.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/al.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-30", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',6,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Europe.", "Landscape: Bohemia in the west consists of rolling plains, hills, and plateaus surrounded by low mountains; Moravia in the east consists of very hilly country.", "Capital: Prague.", "The name begins with Cz and has 14 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Czech Republic", "aliases": ["Czech Republic", "Czechia", "Česko"], "explanation": "At the close of World War I, the Czechs and Slovaks of the former Austro-Hungarian Empire merged to form Czechoslovakia, a parliamentarian democracy.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ez.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-31", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Asia.", "Landscape: mostly hills and mountains; wide coastal plains in west and south.", "Capital: Seoul.", "The name begins with So and has 11 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "South Korea", "aliases": ["South Korea", "Republic of Korea"], "explanation": "By the 5th century CE, Kogoryo emerged as the most powerful, with control over much of the Peninsula and part of Manchuria (modern-day northeast China).", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/ks.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-32", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Europe.", "Landscape: central Transylvanian Basin is separated from the Moldavian Plateau on the east by the Eastern Carpathian Mountains and separated from the Walachian Plain on the south by the Transylvanian Alps.", "Capital: Bucharest.", "The name begins with Ro and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Romania", "aliases": ["Romania"], "explanation": "The principalities of Wallachia and Moldavia -- for centuries under the control of the Turkish Ottoman Empire -- secured their autonomy through the Treaty of Paris in 1856.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ro.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-33", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Northern Africa.", "Landscape: mostly barren, flat to undulating plains, plateaus, depressions.", "Capital: Tripoli (Tarabulus).", "The name begins with Li and has 5 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Libya", "aliases": ["Libya"], "explanation": "Berbers have inhabited central north Africa since ancient times, but Phoenicians, Greeks, Carthaginians, Persians, Egyptians, Romans, and Vandals have all settled and ruled the region.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ly.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-34", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Micronesia.", "Landscape: sandy beach rises to fertile ring around raised coral reefs with phosphate plateau in center.", "Capital: no official capital; government offices in the Yaren District.", "The name begins with Na and has 5 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Nauru", "aliases": ["Nauru", "Republic of Nauru"], "explanation": "By 1000 BCE, Micronesian and Polynesian settlers inhabited Nauru, and the island was divided among 12 clans.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/nr.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-35", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',7,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: South-Eastern Asia.", "Landscape: mountainous.", "Capital: Dili.", "The name begins with Ea and has 10 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "East Timor", "aliases": ["East Timor", "Timor-Leste", "Democratic Republic of Timor-Leste", "Timor Leste"], "explanation": "The island of Timor was actively involved in Southeast Asian trading networks for centuries, and by the 14th century, it exported sandalwood, slaves, honey, and wax.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/tt.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-36", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Africa.", "Landscape: predominately desert plains and sand dunes; flat to rolling plains in south; hills in north.", "Capital: Niamey.", "The name begins with Ni and has 5 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Niger", "aliases": ["Niger", "Republic of Niger"], "explanation": "The Taureg kingdom of Takedda was one of the largest kingdoms in the north and played a prominent role in regional trade in the 14th century.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ng.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-37", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Asia.", "Landscape: flat coral atolls, with white sandy beaches; sits atop the submarine volcanic Chagos-Laccadive Ridge.", "Capital: Malé.", "The name begins with Ma and has 8 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Maldives", "aliases": ["Maldives", "Republic of Maldives"], "explanation": "A sultanate since the 12th century, the Maldives became a British protectorate in 1887 and a republic in 1968, three years after independence.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-asia/mv.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-38", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Europe.", "Landscape: mountainous with ranges extending into the sea as peninsulas or chains of islands.", "Capital: Athens.", "The name begins with Gr and has 6 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Greece", "aliases": ["Greece", "Hellenic Republic"], "explanation": "Greece won independence from the Ottoman Empire in 1830 and became a kingdom.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/gr.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-39", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: South America.", "Landscape: mostly flat to rolling lowlands in north; some plains, hills, mountains, and narrow coastal belt.", "Capital: Brasília.", "The name begins with Br and has 6 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Brazil", "aliases": ["Brazil", "Federative Republic of Brazil"], "explanation": "After more than three centuries under Portuguese rule, Brazil gained its independence in 1822, maintaining a monarchical system of government until the abolition of slavery in 1888 and the subsequent proclamation of a republic by the military in 1889.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/br.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-40", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',8,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Micronesia.", "Landscape: mostly low-lying coral atolls surrounded by extensive reefs.", "Capital: Tarawa.", "The name begins with Ki and has 8 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Kiribati", "aliases": ["Kiribati", "Republic of Kiribati"], "explanation": "The first Austronesian voyagers arrived in the Gilbert Islands as early as 3000 BCE, but these islands were not widely settled until about CE 200 by Micronesians.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/kr.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-41", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Asia.", "Landscape: narrow coastal plain backed by flat-topped hills and rugged mountains; dissected upland desert plains in center slope into the desert interior of the Arabian Peninsula.", "Capital: Sanaa.", "The name begins with Ye and has 5 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Yemen", "aliases": ["Yemen", "Republic of Yemen"], "explanation": "The Kingdom of Yemen (colloquially known as North Yemen) became independent from the Ottoman Empire in 1918 and in 1962 became the Yemen Arab Republic.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/ym.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-42", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Africa.", "Landscape: hilly and mountainous, dropping to a plateau in east, some plains.", "Capital: Gitega (political capital), Bujumbura (commercial capital).", "The name begins with Bu and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Burundi", "aliases": ["Burundi", "Republic of Burundi"], "explanation": "German colonial rule in the late 19th and early 20th centuries and Belgian rule after World War I preserved Burundi’s monarchy.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/by.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-43", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Asia.", "Landscape: central plain with mountains to north and south; scattered but significant plains along southern coast.", "Capital: Nicosia (Lefkosia/Lefkosa).", "The name begins with Cy and has 6 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Cyprus", "aliases": ["Cyprus", "Republic of Cyprus"], "explanation": "A former British colony, Cyprus became independent in 1960 after years of resistance to British rule.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/cy.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-44", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Asia.", "Landscape: mostly rugged and mountainous.", "Capital: Tokyo.", "The name begins with Ja and has 5 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Japan", "aliases": ["Japan"], "explanation": "The Tokugawa shogunate, a hereditary military government, began in 1603 after decades of civil war. More than two centuries of relative stability helped Japanese arts and urban culture flourish.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/ja.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-45", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',9,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Africa.", "Landscape: vast interior plateau rimmed by rugged hills and narrow coastal plain.", "Capital: Pretoria (administrative capital); Cape Town (legislative capital); Bloemfontein (judicial capital).", "The name begins with So and has 12 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "South Africa", "aliases": ["South Africa", "Republic of South Africa"], "explanation": "Dutch traders landed at the southern tip of present-day South Africa in 1652 and established a stopover point on the spice route between the Netherlands and the Far East, founding the city of Cape Town.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/sf.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-46", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Europe.", "Landscape: large, flat to dissected plateau surrounded by rugged hills; Pyrenees Mountains in north.", "Capital: Madrid.", "The name begins with Sp and has 5 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Spain", "aliases": ["Spain", "Kingdom of Spain"], "explanation": "Spain''s powerful world empire of the 16th and 17th centuries ultimately yielded command of the seas to England.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/sp.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-47", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: South America.", "Landscape: rich plains of the Pampas in northern half, flat to rolling plateau of Patagonia in south, rugged Andes along western border.", "Capital: Buenos Aires.", "The name begins with Ar and has 9 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Argentina", "aliases": ["Argentina", "Argentine Republic"], "explanation": "In 1816, the United Provinces of the Río de la Plata declared their independence from Spain.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/ar.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-48", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Europe.", "Landscape: rugged mountains.", "Capital: San Marino (city).", "The name begins with Sa and has 10 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "San Marino", "aliases": ["San Marino", "Republic of San Marino"], "explanation": "San Marino traces its founding to Marinus, a Christian stonemason said to have established a community in 301 CE. This is a founding tradition, rather than a securely documented date.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/sm.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-49", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Europe.", "Landscape: the west-flowing Tagus River divides the country: the north is mountainous toward the interior, while the south is characterized by rolling plains.", "Capital: Lisbon.", "The name begins with Po and has 8 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Portugal", "aliases": ["Portugal", "Portuguese Republic"], "explanation": "A global maritime power during the 15th and 16th centuries, Portugal lost much of its wealth and status with the destruction of Lisbon in a 1755 earthquake, occupation during the Napoleonic Wars, and the independence of Brazil, its wealthiest colony, in 1822.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/po.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-50", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',10,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Asia.", "Landscape: mostly mountainous with some fertile valleys and savanna.", "Capital: Thimphu.", "The name begins with Bh and has 6 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Bhutan", "aliases": ["Bhutan", "Kingdom of Bhutan"], "explanation": "After Britain’s victory in the 1865 Duar War, Britain and Bhutan signed the Treaty of Sinchulu, under which Bhutan would receive an annual subsidy in exchange for ceding land to British India.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-asia/bt.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-51", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Asia.", "Landscape: mostly sandy desert.", "Capital: Riyadh.", "The name begins with Sa and has 12 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Saudi Arabia", "aliases": ["Saudi Arabia", "Kingdom of Saudi Arabia"], "explanation": "After Iraq invaded Kuwait in 1990, Saudi Arabia took in the Kuwaiti royal family and 400,000 refugees, while allowing Western and Arab troops to deploy on its soil and liberate Kuwait the following year.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/sa.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-52", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Asia.", "Landscape: mostly low, flat to rolling plain; mountains in south-central interior.", "Capital: Colombo (commercial capital); Sri Jayewardenepura Kotte (legislative capital).", "The name begins with Sr and has 9 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Sri Lanka", "aliases": ["Sri Lanka", "Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka"], "explanation": "The first Sinhalese arrived in Sri Lanka late in the 6th century BCE, probably from northern India.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-asia/ce.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-53", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Europe.", "Landscape: extremely varied; to the north, rich fertile plains; to the east, limestone ranges and basins; to the southeast, ancient mountains and hills.", "Capital: Belgrade (Beograd).", "The name begins with Se and has 6 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Serbia", "aliases": ["Serbia", "Republic of Serbia"], "explanation": "In 1918, the Croats, Serbs, and Slovenes formed a kingdom known after 1929 as Yugoslavia.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ri.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-54", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Southern Asia.", "Landscape: mostly flat alluvial plain; hilly in southeast.", "Capital: Dhaka.", "The name begins with Ba and has 10 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Bangladesh", "aliases": ["Bangladesh", "People''s Republic of Bangladesh"], "explanation": "The huge delta region at the confluence of the Ganges and Brahmaputra River systems -- now referred to as Bangladesh -- was a loosely incorporated outpost of various empires for much of the first millennium CE Muslim conversions and settlement in the region began in the 10th century, primarily from Arab and Persian traders and preachers.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-asia/bg.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-55", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',11,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Asia.", "Landscape: mostly hills and mountains separated by deep, narrow valleys; wide coastal plains in west, discontinuous in east.", "Capital: Pyongyang.", "The name begins with No and has 11 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "North Korea", "aliases": ["North Korea", "Dem. Rep. Korea", "Democratic People''s Republic of Korea", "DPRK"], "explanation": "By the 5th century CE, Kogoryo emerged as the most powerful, with control over much of the Peninsula and part of Manchuria (modern-day northeast China).", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/kn.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-56", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Africa.", "Landscape: mostly barren, flat plains of the Sahara; some central hills.", "Capital: Nouakchott.", "The name begins with Ma and has 10 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Mauritania", "aliases": ["Mauritania", "Islamic Republic of Mauritania"], "explanation": "The remainder of Mauritania’s ethnic groups derive from Sub-Saharan ethnic groups originating mainly from the Senegal River Valley, including descendants of former enslaved peoples.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/mr.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-57", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: South-Eastern Asia.", "Landscape: low, flat delta in south and north; central highlands; hilly, mountainous in far north and northwest.", "Capital: Hanoi (Ha Noi).", "The name begins with Vi and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Vietnam", "aliases": ["Vietnam", "Socialist Republic of Vietnam", "Viet Nam"], "explanation": "Vietnam''s early history included periods of occupation by outside forces and eventual power consolidation under Vietnamese dynastic families.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/vm.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-58", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Caribbean.", "Landscape: volcanic and mountainous with broad, fertile valleys.", "Capital: Castries.", "The name begins with Sa and has 11 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Saint Lucia", "aliases": ["Saint Lucia"], "explanation": "England and France contested Saint Lucia -- with its fine natural harbor at Castries and burgeoning sugar industry -- throughout the 17th and early 18th centuries, with possession changing 14 times; it was finally ceded to the UK in 1814 and became part of the British Windward Islands colony.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/st.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-59", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Middle Africa.", "Landscape: narrow coastal plain rises abruptly to vast interior plateau.", "Capital: Luanda.", "The name begins with An and has 6 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Angola", "aliases": ["Angola", "People''s Republic of Angola"], "explanation": "Bantu-speaking people settled in the area now called Angola in 6th century CE; by the 10th century various Bantu groups had established kingdoms, of which Kongo became the most powerful.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ao.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-60", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',12,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Africa.", "Landscape: mostly flat to undulating plain; some hills and low mountains.", "Capital: Porto-Novo (constitutional capital); Cotonou (seat of government).", "The name begins with Be and has 5 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Benin", "aliases": ["Benin", "Republic of Benin"], "explanation": "The Kingdom of Dahomey emerged on the Abomey plateau in the 17th century and was a regional power for much of the 18th and 19th centuries.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/bn.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-61", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Europe.", "Landscape: rugged mountains in the central and northern part and lowlands in the south.", "Capital: Bratislava.", "The name begins with Sl and has 8 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Slovakia", "aliases": ["Slovakia", "Slovak Republic"], "explanation": "Slovakia traces its roots to the 9th century state of Great Moravia.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/lo.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-62", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Africa.", "Landscape: mostly plateau with rim of mountains.", "Capital: Kampala.", "The name begins with Ug and has 6 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Uganda", "aliases": ["Uganda", "Republic of Uganda"], "explanation": "An ancient crossroads for various migrations, Uganda has as many as 65 ethnic groups that speak languages from three of Africa’s four major linguistic families.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ug.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-63", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Caribbean.", "Landscape: volcanic in origin with central mountains.", "Capital: Saint George''s.", "The name begins with Gr and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Grenada", "aliases": ["Grenada"], "explanation": "The French settled Grenada in the 17th century, established sugar estates, and imported large numbers of African slaves.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/gj.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-64", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Europe.", "Landscape: mostly mountains with lowlands in north and southeast.", "Capital: Sofia.", "The name begins with Bu and has 8 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Bulgaria", "aliases": ["Bulgaria", "Republic of Bulgaria"], "explanation": "The Bulgars, a Central Asian Turkic tribe, merged with the local Slavic inhabitants in the late 7th century to form the first Bulgarian state.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/bu.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-65", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('clue-cascade',13,1,'[{"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Western Africa.", "Landscape: flood plain of the Gambia River flanked by some low hills.", "Capital: Banjul.", "The name begins with Th and has 10 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "The Gambia", "aliases": ["The Gambia", "Gambia", "Republic of the Gambia"], "explanation": "In the 10th century, Muslim merchants established some of The Gambia’s earliest large settlements as trans-Saharan trade hubs.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ga.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-66", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Europe.", "Landscape: broad plain with low hills west of Urals; vast coniferous forest and tundra in Siberia; uplands and mountains along southern border regions.", "Capital: Moscow.", "The name begins with Ru and has 6 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Russia", "aliases": ["Russia", "Russian Federation"], "explanation": "Founded in the 12th century, the Principality of Muscovy emerged from over 200 years of Mongol domination (13th-15th centuries) and gradually conquered and absorbed surrounding principalities.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-asia/rs.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-67", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Eastern Africa.", "Landscape: mostly flat to undulating plateau rising to hills in north.", "Capital: Mogadishu.", "The name begins with So and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Somalia", "aliases": ["Somalia", "Federal Republic of Somalia"], "explanation": "Between CE 800 and 1100, immigrant Muslim Arabs and Persians set up coastal trading posts along the Gulf of Aden and the Indian Ocean, solidifying present-day Somalia’s close trading relationship with the Arab Peninsula.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/so.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-68", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Micronesia.", "Landscape: low coral limestone and sand islands.", "Capital: Majuro.", "The name begins with Ma and has 16 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Marshall Islands", "aliases": ["Marshall Islands", "Republic of the Marshall Islands"], "explanation": "Humans arrived in the Marshall Islands in the first millennium BCE and gradually created permanent settlements on the various atolls.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/rm.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-69", "version": 1}, {"kind": "clues", "prompt": "Which country am I?", "clues": ["Region: Northern Europe.", "Landscape: mostly plateau interspersed with mountain peaks, icefields; coast deeply indented by bays and fiords.", "Capital: Reykjavik.", "The name begins with Ic and has 7 characters (including spaces)."], "answer": "Iceland", "aliases": ["Iceland", "Republic of Iceland"], "explanation": "Settled by Norwegian and Celtic (Scottish and Irish) immigrants during the late 9th and 10th centuries CE, Iceland boasts the world''s oldest functioning legislative assembly, the Althingi, which was established in 930.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ic.json"], "id": "clue-cascade-70", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',0,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Djibouti — In [year], the French held a referendum that provided residents of French Somaliland the option to either continue their association with France or to join neighboring Somalia as it established its independence."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Equatorial Guinea — In [year], Portugal ceded its colonial hold over present-day Equatorial Guinea to Spain in the Treaty of El Pardo."}, {"id": "2", "label": "Philippines — In [year], the Philippines became a self-governing commonwealth."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Solomon Islands — The islands were granted self-government in [year] and independence two years later under Prime Minister Sir Peter Kenilorea."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Paraguay — Paraguay achieved its independence from Spain in [year] with the help of neighboring states."}], "answer": ["1", "4", "2", "0", "3"], "explanation": "1778 · Equatorial Guinea — In [year], Portugal ceded its colonial hold over present-day Equatorial Guinea to Spain in the Treaty of El Pardo.\n1811 · Paraguay — Paraguay achieved its independence from Spain in [year] with the help of neighboring states.\n1935 · Philippines — In [year], the Philippines became a self-governing commonwealth.\n1958 · Djibouti — In [year], the French held a referendum that provided residents of French Somaliland the option to either continue their association with France or to join neighboring Somalia as it established its independence.\n1976 · Solomon Islands — The islands were granted self-government in [year] and independence two years later under Prime Minister Sir Peter Kenilorea.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/bp.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/ek.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/pa.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/rp.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/dj.json"], "id": "before-or-after-1", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',1,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Ethiopia — Many Ethiopians still speak reverently about the Battle of Adwa in [year], when they defeated Italian forces and won their freedom from colonial rule."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Philippines — In [year], the Philippines became a self-governing commonwealth."}, {"id": "2", "label": "Belarus — In [year], Belarus and Russia signed a treaty on a two-state union, envisioning greater political and economic integration."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Republic of the Congo — Upon independence in [year], the former French region of Middle Congo became the Republic of the Congo."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Philippines — On 4 July [year] the Republic of the Philippines attained its independence."}], "answer": ["0", "1", "4", "3", "2"], "explanation": "1896 · Ethiopia — Many Ethiopians still speak reverently about the Battle of Adwa in [year], when they defeated Italian forces and won their freedom from colonial rule.\n1935 · Philippines — In [year], the Philippines became a self-governing commonwealth.\n1946 · Philippines — On 4 July [year] the Republic of the Philippines attained its independence.\n1960 · Republic of the Congo — Upon independence in [year], the former French region of Middle Congo became the Republic of the Congo.\n1999 · Belarus — In [year], Belarus and Russia signed a treaty on a two-state union, envisioning greater political and economic integration.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/rp.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/et.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/bo.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/cf.json"], "id": "before-or-after-2", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',2,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Türkiye — The Kurdistan Workers'' Party (PKK), a US-designated terrorist organization, began a separatist insurgency in Turkey in [year], and the struggle has long dominated the attention of Turkish security forces."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Philippines — On 4 July [year] the Republic of the Philippines attained its independence."}, {"id": "2", "label": "Monaco — The Genoese built a fortress on the site of present-day Monaco in [year]."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Vanuatu — From [year], Britain and France jointly administered the New Hebrides, now Vanuatu."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Panama — With US backing, Panama seceded from Colombia in [year] and promptly signed a treaty with the US allowing for the construction of a canal and US sovereignty over a strip of land known as the Panama Canal Zone on either side of the structure."}], "answer": ["2", "4", "3", "1", "0"], "explanation": "1215 · Monaco — The Genoese built a fortress on the site of present-day Monaco in [year].\n1903 · Panama — With US backing, Panama seceded from Colombia in [year] and promptly signed a treaty with the US allowing for the construction of a canal and US sovereignty over a strip of land known as the Panama Canal Zone on either side of the structure.\n1906 · Vanuatu — From [year], Britain and France jointly administered the New Hebrides, now Vanuatu.\n1946 · Philippines — On 4 July [year] the Republic of the Philippines attained its independence.\n1984 · Türkiye — The Kurdistan Workers'' Party (PKK), a US-designated terrorist organization, began a separatist insurgency in Turkey in [year], and the struggle has long dominated the attention of Turkish security forces.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/mn.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/tu.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/nh.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/rp.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/pm.json"], "id": "before-or-after-3", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',3,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Zimbabwe — In [year], the government under White Prime Minister Ian Smith unilaterally declared its independence from the UK."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Togo — French Togoland became Togo upon independence in [year]."}, {"id": "2", "label": "Panama — With US backing, Panama seceded from Colombia in [year] and promptly signed a treaty with the US allowing for the construction of a canal and US sovereignty over a strip of land known as the Panama Canal Zone on either side of the structure."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Namibia — Various ethnic groups occupied southwestern Africa prior to Germany establishing a colony over most of the territory in [year]."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Portugal — A revolution deposed the monarchy in [year], and for most of the next six decades, repressive governments ran the country."}], "answer": ["3", "2", "4", "1", "0"], "explanation": "1884 · Namibia — Various ethnic groups occupied southwestern Africa prior to Germany establishing a colony over most of the territory in [year].\n1903 · Panama — With US backing, Panama seceded from Colombia in [year] and promptly signed a treaty with the US allowing for the construction of a canal and US sovereignty over a strip of land known as the Panama Canal Zone on either side of the structure.\n1910 · Portugal — A revolution deposed the monarchy in [year], and for most of the next six decades, repressive governments ran the country.\n1960 · Togo — French Togoland became Togo upon independence in [year].\n1965 · Zimbabwe — In [year], the government under White Prime Minister Ian Smith unilaterally declared its independence from the UK.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/to.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/po.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/wa.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/pm.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/zi.json"], "id": "before-or-after-4", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',4,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Romania — The principalities of Wallachia and Moldavia -- for centuries under the control of the Turkish Ottoman Empire -- secured their autonomy through the Treaty of Paris in [year]."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Andorra — In [year], this feudal system was modified with the introduction of a modern constitution; the co-princes remained as titular heads of state, but the government transformed into a parliamentary democracy."}, {"id": "2", "label": "Ethiopia — Many Ethiopians still speak reverently about the Battle of Adwa in [year], when they defeated Italian forces and won their freedom from colonial rule."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Apollo 11 lands humans on the Moon."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Marshall Islands — Spain formally claimed the islands in [year]."}], "answer": ["4", "0", "2", "3", "1"], "explanation": "1592 · Marshall Islands — Spain formally claimed the islands in [year].\n1856 · Romania — The principalities of Wallachia and Moldavia -- for centuries under the control of the Turkish Ottoman Empire -- secured their autonomy through the Treaty of Paris in [year].\n1896 · Ethiopia — Many Ethiopians still speak reverently about the Battle of Adwa in [year], when they defeated Italian forces and won their freedom from colonial rule.\n1969 · Apollo 11 lands humans on the Moon.\n1993 · Andorra — In [year], this feudal system was modified with the introduction of a modern constitution; the co-princes remained as titular heads of state, but the government transformed into a parliamentary democracy.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/an.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/et.json", "https://www.nasa.gov/mission/apollo-11/", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/rm.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/ro.json"], "id": "before-or-after-5", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',5,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Poland — Solidarity began as an independent trade union in [year] and grew into a political force with more than ten million members, challenging communist rule."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Egypt — The Suez Canal opened in [year], linking the Mediterranean and Red seas and making Egypt a crossroads of global shipping."}, {"id": "2", "label": "Japan — The Treaty of Kanagawa opened Japanese ports to the United States in [year]."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Iraq — Iraq attained its independence as a kingdom in [year]."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Switzerland — The Swiss Confederation was founded in [year] as a defensive alliance among three cantons."}], "answer": ["4", "2", "1", "3", "0"], "explanation": "1291 · Switzerland — The Swiss Confederation was founded in [year] as a defensive alliance among three cantons.\n1854 · Japan — The Treaty of Kanagawa opened Japanese ports to the United States in [year].\n1869 · Egypt — The Suez Canal opened in [year], linking the Mediterranean and Red seas and making Egypt a crossroads of global shipping.\n1932 · Iraq — Iraq attained its independence as a kingdom in [year].\n1980 · Poland — Solidarity began as an independent trade union in [year] and grew into a political force with more than ten million members, challenging communist rule.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/pl.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/eg.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/sz.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/ja.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/iz.json"], "id": "before-or-after-6", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',6,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Egypt — The Suez Canal opened in [year], linking the Mediterranean and Red seas and making Egypt a crossroads of global shipping."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Honduras — Hurricane Mitch devastated the country in [year], killing about 5,600 people and causing approximately $2 billion in damage."}, {"id": "2", "label": "Panama — With US backing, Panama seceded from Colombia in [year] and promptly signed a treaty with the US allowing for the construction of a canal and US sovereignty over a strip of land known as the Panama Canal Zone on either side of the structure."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Apollo 11 lands humans on the Moon."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Eritrea — Ethiopia''s full annexation of Eritrea as a province 10 years later sparked a violent 30-year conflict for independence that ended in [year] with Eritrean fighters defeating government forces."}], "answer": ["0", "2", "3", "4", "1"], "explanation": "1869 · Egypt — The Suez Canal opened in [year], linking the Mediterranean and Red seas and making Egypt a crossroads of global shipping.\n1903 · Panama — With US backing, Panama seceded from Colombia in [year] and promptly signed a treaty with the US allowing for the construction of a canal and US sovereignty over a strip of land known as the Panama Canal Zone on either side of the structure.\n1969 · Apollo 11 lands humans on the Moon.\n1991 · Eritrea — Ethiopia''s full annexation of Eritrea as a province 10 years later sparked a violent 30-year conflict for independence that ended in [year] with Eritrean fighters defeating government forces.\n1998 · Honduras — Hurricane Mitch devastated the country in [year], killing about 5,600 people and causing approximately $2 billion in damage.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/er.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/eg.json", "https://www.nasa.gov/mission/apollo-11/", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/ho.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/pm.json"], "id": "before-or-after-7", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',7,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Paraguay — Paraguay achieved its independence from Spain in [year] with the help of neighboring states."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Luxembourg — When Belgium declared independence from the Netherlands in [year], Luxembourg lost more than half of its territory to Belgium but gained a larger measure of autonomy within the Kingdom of the Netherlands."}, {"id": "2", "label": "North Macedonia — The country was eventually admitted to the UN in [year] as \"The former Yugoslav Republic of Macedonia,\" and at the same time it agreed to UN-sponsored negotiations on the name dispute."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Germany — With the advent of the Cold War, two German states were formed in [year]: the western Federal Republic of Germany (FRG) and the eastern German Democratic Republic (GDR)."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Mauritius — The Dutch abandoned their financially distressed settlement in [year], although a number of formerly enslaved people remained."}], "answer": ["4", "0", "1", "3", "2"], "explanation": "1710 · Mauritius — The Dutch abandoned their financially distressed settlement in [year], although a number of formerly enslaved people remained.\n1811 · Paraguay — Paraguay achieved its independence from Spain in [year] with the help of neighboring states.\n1839 · Luxembourg — When Belgium declared independence from the Netherlands in [year], Luxembourg lost more than half of its territory to Belgium but gained a larger measure of autonomy within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\n1949 · Germany — With the advent of the Cold War, two German states were formed in [year]: the western Federal Republic of Germany (FRG) and the eastern German Democratic Republic (GDR).\n1993 · North Macedonia — The country was eventually admitted to the UN in [year] as \"The former Yugoslav Republic of Macedonia,\" and at the same time it agreed to UN-sponsored negotiations on the name dispute.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/gm.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/mp.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/mk.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/pa.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/lu.json"], "id": "before-or-after-8", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',8,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Honduras — Hurricane Mitch devastated the country in [year], killing about 5,600 people and causing approximately $2 billion in damage."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Kuwait — Iraq attacked and overran Kuwait in [year]."}, {"id": "2", "label": "Belarus — In [year], Belarus and Russia signed a treaty on a two-state union, envisioning greater political and economic integration."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Monaco — The Genoese built a fortress on the site of present-day Monaco in [year]."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Portugal — A revolution deposed the monarchy in [year], and for most of the next six decades, repressive governments ran the country."}], "answer": ["3", "4", "1", "0", "2"], "explanation": "1215 · Monaco — The Genoese built a fortress on the site of present-day Monaco in [year].\n1910 · Portugal — A revolution deposed the monarchy in [year], and for most of the next six decades, repressive governments ran the country.\n1990 · Kuwait — Iraq attacked and overran Kuwait in [year].\n1998 · Honduras — Hurricane Mitch devastated the country in [year], killing about 5,600 people and causing approximately $2 billion in damage.\n1999 · Belarus — In [year], Belarus and Russia signed a treaty on a two-state union, envisioning greater political and economic integration.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/mn.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/po.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/bo.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/ho.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/ku.json"], "id": "before-or-after-9", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',9,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Bolivia — Democratic civilian rule was established in [year], but leaders have faced problems of deep-seated poverty, social unrest, and illegal drug production."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Kuwait — Iraq attacked and overran Kuwait in [year]."}, {"id": "2", "label": "Mauritius — The Dutch abandoned their financially distressed settlement in [year], although a number of formerly enslaved people remained."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Papua New Guinea — In [year], PNG gained independence and became a member of the Commonwealth."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Mauritius — In [year], the French established what would become a highly profitable settlement focused on sugar cane plantations that were reliant on the labor of enslaved people brought to Mauritius from other parts of Africa."}], "answer": ["2", "4", "3", "0", "1"], "explanation": "1710 · Mauritius — The Dutch abandoned their financially distressed settlement in [year], although a number of formerly enslaved people remained.\n1722 · Mauritius — In [year], the French established what would become a highly profitable settlement focused on sugar cane plantations that were reliant on the labor of enslaved people brought to Mauritius from other parts of Africa.\n1975 · Papua New Guinea — In [year], PNG gained independence and became a member of the Commonwealth.\n1982 · Bolivia — Democratic civilian rule was established in [year], but leaders have faced problems of deep-seated poverty, social unrest, and illegal drug production.\n1990 · Kuwait — Iraq attacked and overran Kuwait in [year].", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/pp.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/mp.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-america/bl.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/ku.json"], "id": "before-or-after-10", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',10,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Djibouti — In [year], the French held a referendum that provided residents of French Somaliland the option to either continue their association with France or to join neighboring Somalia as it established its independence."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Burundi — Burundi gained its independence from Belgium in [year] as the Kingdom of Burundi."}, {"id": "2", "label": "Solomon Islands — The islands were granted self-government in [year] and independence two years later under Prime Minister Sir Peter Kenilorea."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Antigua and Barbuda — The islands became an independent state within the British Commonwealth of Nations in [year]."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Luxembourg — When Belgium declared independence from the Netherlands in [year], Luxembourg lost more than half of its territory to Belgium but gained a larger measure of autonomy within the Kingdom of the Netherlands."}], "answer": ["4", "0", "1", "2", "3"], "explanation": "1839 · Luxembourg — When Belgium declared independence from the Netherlands in [year], Luxembourg lost more than half of its territory to Belgium but gained a larger measure of autonomy within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\n1958 · Djibouti — In [year], the French held a referendum that provided residents of French Somaliland the option to either continue their association with France or to join neighboring Somalia as it established its independence.\n1962 · Burundi — Burundi gained its independence from Belgium in [year] as the Kingdom of Burundi.\n1976 · Solomon Islands — The islands were granted self-government in [year] and independence two years later under Prime Minister Sir Peter Kenilorea.\n1981 · Antigua and Barbuda — The islands became an independent state within the British Commonwealth of Nations in [year].", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/australia-oceania/bp.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/by.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/dj.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/lu.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/ac.json"], "id": "before-or-after-11", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',11,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Honduras — Once part of Spain''s vast empire in the New World, Honduras became an independent nation in [year]."}, {"id": "1", "label": "El Salvador — A 12-year civil war, which cost about 75,000 lives, was brought to a close in [year] when the government and leftist rebels signed a treaty that provided for military and political reforms."}, {"id": "2", "label": "Ethiopia — However, in [year], a military junta called the Derg deposed him and established a socialist state."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Myanmar — Burma gained full independence in [year]."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Norway — In [year], Norway was absorbed into a union with Denmark that lasted more than four centuries."}], "answer": ["4", "0", "3", "2", "1"], "explanation": "1397 · Norway — In [year], Norway was absorbed into a union with Denmark that lasted more than four centuries.\n1821 · Honduras — Once part of Spain''s vast empire in the New World, Honduras became an independent nation in [year].\n1948 · Myanmar — Burma gained full independence in [year].\n1974 · Ethiopia — However, in [year], a military junta called the Derg deposed him and established a socialist state.\n1992 · El Salvador — A 12-year civil war, which cost about 75,000 lives, was brought to a close in [year] when the government and leftist rebels signed a treaty that provided for military and political reforms.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/no.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/et.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/es.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/ho.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/bm.json"], "id": "before-or-after-12", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',12,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Alan Shepard becomes the first American in space."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Iran — The US cut off diplomatic relations with Iran in April [year]."}, {"id": "2", "label": "Afghanistan — The Soviet Union invaded in [year] to support the tottering Afghan communist regime, touching off a long and destructive war."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Djibouti — In [year], the French held a referendum that provided residents of French Somaliland the option to either continue their association with France or to join neighboring Somalia as it established its independence."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Trinidad and Tobago — Trinidad and Tobago attained independence in [year]."}], "answer": ["3", "0", "4", "2", "1"], "explanation": "1958 · Djibouti — In [year], the French held a referendum that provided residents of French Somaliland the option to either continue their association with France or to join neighboring Somalia as it established its independence.\n1961 · Alan Shepard becomes the first American in space.\n1962 · Trinidad and Tobago — Trinidad and Tobago attained independence in [year].\n1979 · Afghanistan — The Soviet Union invaded in [year] to support the tottering Afghan communist regime, touching off a long and destructive war.\n1980 · Iran — The US cut off diplomatic relations with Iran in April [year].", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/ir.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/dj.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/south-asia/af.json", "https://www.nasa.gov/history/may-5-1961-alan-shepard-becomes-the-first-american-in-space/", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/central-america-n-caribbean/td.json"], "id": "before-or-after-13", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('before-or-after',13,1,'[{"kind": "timeline", "prompt": "Arrange these moments from earliest to latest.", "cards": [{"id": "0", "label": "Taiwan — In [year], military defeat forced China''s Qing Dynasty to cede Taiwan to Japan, which then governed Taiwan for 50 years."}, {"id": "1", "label": "Norway — In [year], Norway was absorbed into a union with Denmark that lasted more than four centuries."}, {"id": "2", "label": "South Sudan — When Sudan gained its independence in [year], the southern region received assurances that it would participate fully in the political system."}, {"id": "3", "label": "Iraq — Iraq attained its independence as a kingdom in [year]."}, {"id": "4", "label": "Cameroon — French Cameroon became independent in [year] as the Republic of Cameroon."}], "answer": ["1", "0", "3", "2", "4"], "explanation": "1397 · Norway — In [year], Norway was absorbed into a union with Denmark that lasted more than four centuries.\n1895 · Taiwan — In [year], military defeat forced China''s Qing Dynasty to cede Taiwan to Japan, which then governed Taiwan for 50 years.\n1932 · Iraq — Iraq attained its independence as a kingdom in [year].\n1956 · South Sudan — When Sudan gained its independence in [year], the southern region received assurances that it would participate fully in the political system.\n1960 · Cameroon — French Cameroon became independent in [year] as the Republic of Cameroon.", "sources": ["https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/od.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/africa/cm.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/europe/no.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/east-n-southeast-asia/tw.json", "https://github.com/factbook/factbook.json/blob/144d6977b2b01ac1cbd220de754c0a005616760b/middle-east/iz.json"], "id": "before-or-after-14", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('how-much-ish',0,1,'[{"kind": "scale", "prompt": "Resize Neptune to its real diameter relative to Saturn (without rings).", "target": {"name": "Neptune", "dimension": "diameter", "shape": "sphere"}, "reference": {"name": "Saturn (without rings)", "dimension": "diameter", "shape": "sphere"}, "bounds": [0.05, 20], "answer": 0.41089798898254465, "explanation": "Neptune: 49,528,000 m diameter. Saturn (without rings): 120,536,000 m diameter. The ratio is 0.411×. Measurements use the source definitions; planetary figures are equatorial diameters.", "sources": ["https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/"], "id": "how-much-ish-1", "version": 1}, {"kind": "scale", "prompt": "Resize Liberty’s hand to its real length relative to Statue of Liberty (base to torch).", "target": {"name": "Liberty’s hand", "dimension": "length", "shape": "hand"}, "reference": {"name": "Statue of Liberty (base to torch)", "dimension": "height", "shape": "statue"}, "bounds": [0.05, 20], "answer": 0.10857763300760044, "explanation": "Liberty’s hand: 5 m length. Statue of Liberty (base to torch): 46 m height. The ratio is 0.109×. Measurements use the source definitions; planetary figures are equatorial diameters.", "sources": ["https://www.nps.gov/stli/learn/historyculture/statue-statistics.htm"], "id": "how-much-ish-2", "version": 1}, {"kind": "scale", "prompt": "Resize Earth to its real diameter relative to Uranus.", "target": {"name": "Earth", "dimension": "diameter", "shape": "sphere"}, "reference": {"name": "Uranus", "dimension": "diameter", "shape": "sphere"}, "bounds": [0.05, 20], "answer": 0.24954027935365233, "explanation": "Earth: 12,756,000 m diameter. Uranus: 51,118,000 m diameter. The ratio is 0.25×. Measurements use the source definitions; planetary figures are equatorial diameters.", "sources": ["https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/"], "id": "how-much-ish-3", "version": 1}, {"kind": "scale", "prompt": "Resize Neptune to its real diameter relative to Mars.", "target": {"name": "Neptune", "dimension": "diameter", "shape": "sphere"}, "reference": {"name": "Mars", "dimension": "diameter", "shape": "sphere"}, "bounds": [0.05, 20], "answer": 7.292108362779741, "explanation": "Neptune: 49,528,000 m diameter. Mars: 6,792,000 m diameter. The ratio is 7.29×. Measurements use the source definitions; planetary figures are equatorial diameters.", "sources": ["https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/"], "id": "how-much-ish-4", "version": 1}, {"kind": "scale", "prompt": "Resize Liberty’s tablet to its real length relative to Statue of Liberty (ground to torch).", "target": {"name": "Liberty’s tablet", "dimension": "length", "shape": "tablet"}, "reference": {"name": "Statue of Liberty (ground to torch)", "dimension": "height", "shape": "statue-base"}, "bounds": [0.05, 20], "answer": 0.0773201419507474, "explanation": "Liberty’s tablet: 7 m length. Statue of Liberty (ground to torch): 93 m height. The ratio is 0.0773×. Measurements use the source definitions; planetary figures are equatorial diameters.", "sources": ["https://www.nps.gov/stli/learn/historyculture/statue-statistics.htm"], "id": "how-much-ish-5", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO ledger_private.trivia_packs VALUES ('how-much-ish',1,1,'[{"kind": "scale", "prompt": "Resize Statue of Liberty (base to torch) to its real height relative to Eiffel Tower (including antennas, 2026 reference).", "target": {"name": "Statue of Liberty (base to torch)", "dimension": "height", "shape": "statue"}, "reference": {"name": "Eiffel Tower (including antennas, 2026 reference)", "dimension": "height", "shape": "tower"}, "bounds": [0.05, 20], "answer": 0.13954545454545453, "explanation": "Statue of Liberty (base to torch): 46 m height. Eiffel Tower (including antennas, 2026 reference): 330 m height. The ratio is 0.14×. Measurements use the source definitions; planetary figures are equatorial diameters.", "sources": ["https://www.nps.gov/stli/learn/historyculture/statue-statistics.htm", "https://www.toureiffel.paris/en/the-monument/key-figures"], "id": "how-much-ish-6", "version": 1}, {"kind": "scale", "prompt": "Resize Earth to its real diameter relative to Moon.", "target": {"name": "Earth", "dimension": "diameter", "shape": "sphere"}, "reference": {"name": "Moon", "dimension": "diameter", "shape": "sphere"}, "bounds": [0.05, 20], "answer": 3.670791366906475, "explanation": "Earth: 12,756,000 m diameter. Moon: 3,475,000 m diameter. The ratio is 3.67×. Measurements use the source definitions; planetary figures are equatorial diameters.", "sources": ["https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/"], "id": "how-much-ish-7", "version": 1}, {"kind": "scale", "prompt": "Resize Liberty’s head (chin to cranium) to its real height relative to Liberty’s hand.", "target": {"name": "Liberty’s head (chin to cranium)", "dimension": "height", "shape": "head"}, "reference": {"name": "Liberty’s hand", "dimension": "length", "shape": "hand"}, "bounds": [0.05, 20], "answer": 1.052, "explanation": "Liberty’s head (chin to cranium): 5 m height. Liberty’s hand: 5 m length. The ratio is 1.05×. Measurements use the source definitions; planetary figures are equatorial diameters.", "sources": ["https://www.nps.gov/stli/learn/historyculture/statue-statistics.htm"], "id": "how-much-ish-8", "version": 1}, {"kind": "scale", "prompt": "Resize Pluto to its real diameter relative to Moon.", "target": {"name": "Pluto", "dimension": "diameter", "shape": "sphere"}, "reference": {"name": "Moon", "dimension": "diameter", "shape": "sphere"}, "bounds": [0.05, 20], "answer": 0.6837410071942446, "explanation": "Pluto: 2,376,000 m diameter. Moon: 3,475,000 m diameter. The ratio is 0.684×. Measurements use the source definitions; planetary figures are equatorial diameters.", "sources": ["https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/"], "id": "how-much-ish-9", "version": 1}, {"kind": "scale", "prompt": "Resize Liberty’s tablet to its real length relative to Liberty’s hand.", "target": {"name": "Liberty’s tablet", "dimension": "length", "shape": "tablet"}, "reference": {"name": "Liberty’s hand", "dimension": "length", "shape": "hand"}, "bounds": [0.05, 20], "answer": 1.4380000000000002, "explanation": "Liberty’s tablet: 7 m length. Liberty’s hand: 5 m length. The ratio is 1.44×. Measurements use the source definitions; planetary figures are equatorial diameters.", "sources": ["https://www.nps.gov/stli/learn/historyculture/statue-statistics.htm"], "id": "how-much-ish-10", "version": 1}]'::jsonb);
